--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled material (vendored byte-for-byte; sha256-pinned in _vendor/SHA256SUMS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- src/skeleton_key_optimizer/_vendor/pyrit/datasets/executors/skeleton_key/skeleton_key.prompt
    The Skeleton Key preamble seed (SeedDataset YAML), read verbatim.
- src/skeleton_key_optimizer/_vendor/pyrit/datasets/executors/skeleton_key/skeleton_key_acceptance.prompt
    The simulated-acceptance seed (SeedDataset YAML), read verbatim.

The attack control flow (event mapping, surface selection, transcript framing)
is reimplemented from scratch in src/skeleton_key_optimizer/ (original to this
module, MIT); no prompt/dataset body is reproduced in authored code.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Technique / citation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Skeleton Key has no academic paper. It was disclosed by Microsoft:

    Mark Russinovich, "Mitigating Skeleton Key, a new type of generative AI
    jailbreak technique," Microsoft, 2024.

When reporting numbers produced with this module, cite the Microsoft Skeleton
Key disclosure and Microsoft PyRIT at the pinned commit above.
